595→### Animated sine wave ripples [Needs Review] [[Ep5, 66:20](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qPwiuQUT-N4&t=3980s)]
596→```vex
597→int pts[];
598→int pt;
599→vector pos;
600→float d, w;
601→
602→pts = nearpoints(1, @P, ch('radius'), chi('number_of_points'));
603→
604→pt = pts[0];
605→pos = point(1, 'P', pt);
606→d = distance(@P, pos);
607→w = d * ch('freq');
608→w = @Frame * ch('speed');
609→w = sin(w);
610→w *= ch('amp');
611→w = fit(d, 0, ch('radius'), 1, 0);
612→@P.y += w;
613→```
614→Creates animated sine wave ripples by finding nearby points and using their distance to modulate a time-based sine wave that displaces points vertically. The wave amplitude is attenuated based on distance using fit(), and the animation is driven by @Frame. Multiple parameters control radius, frequency, speed, and amplitude of the ripples.
