964→### Circular Path with Sine and Cosine [[Ep8, 35:06](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KJUZD4PTyz0&t=2106s)]
965→```vex
966→vector uv;
967→
968→uv.x = sin(@Time*2);
969→uv.y = cos(@Time*2);
970→
971→uv = fit(uv, -1, 1, -0.2, 0.2);
972→
973→@P = primv(1, 'P', 0, uv);
974→@N = primv(1, 'N', 0, uv);
975→```
976→Creates circular motion by using sine and cosine functions on the same time value for UV coordinates, then uses fit() to scale the range from [-1,1] to [-0.2,0.2]. The scaled UV coordinates are used with primv() to sample position and normal attributes from the second input, creating a point that moves in a circular path across a primitive's parametric space.
